From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:10:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] include: Make msinkaut.idl match the Tablet PC SDK.

IInkRectangle had no base interface, so every method of its vtable was
seven places early; it derives from IDispatch.  The device context of
IInkRenderer's methods and IInkCollector's window are LONG_PTR, as a
64-bit handle needs.  IInkStrokeDisp's identifier is ID, as the SDK
names it.  The collections' _NewEnum and Item carry DISPID_NEWENUM and
DISPID_VALUE, without which For Each and default members fail from
script, and IInkExtendedProperties, IInkStrokes, IInkCustomStrokes,
IInkDisp and IInkRenderer carry the SDK's dispatch ids instead of
generated ones.  The layouts were checked against the Win32 metadata of
the SDK, and the new coclasses' CLSIDs against Office's own modules,
which use them: InkRenderer, InkDrawingAttributes, InkTransform and
InkRectangle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

